What is Composite Rebar?
Composite rebar refers to reinforcement bars composed of high strength fibers such as glass, carbon or basalt embedded in a polymer resin matrix. This lightweight alternative offers superior corrosion resistance, reduced maintenance costs, and lower embodied carbon compared to conventional steel reinforcement. By integrating these fibers into concrete, composite rebar delivers enhanced tensile performance while significantly decreasing the overall weight of infrastructure, thus enabling longer spans and more efficient design solutions.
